      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-13T19:33:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Coudn\u0027t we solve that with a #pragma around the memset to avoid the compiler optimizing it out?\n\nIt\u0027s tricky to get right, so we rely on canonical implementations rather than re-implementing it everywhere it\u0027s needed.\n\nWe do have a C version that can be used: `OPENSSL_cleanse`. The C++ version is nice because it leverages RAII to make sure that all return paths are covered.\n\nHere\u0027s an [example](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/fpsensor/fpsensor.cc;l\u003d573-578;drc\u003d1285bf7bb93a88bef3432b30e4b6a14bb18cc985).",
      "parentUuid": "fb997557_92664c76",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "fab91b49fe966c809766e658498925ae0ab3e1b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
